@@ -118,17 +118,19 @@ ### Ordering and Fairness
 
 The **next candidate queue** is **deterministic**: same state input → same next ticket, no random draw.
 
+**Implementation (`App\Actions\CallNextTicket`):** a ticket is **normal** when `priority = 0` and **priority** when `priority > 0` (higher value = more important). Only `waiting` tickets of the given queue are candidates; tickets of other queues are never selected and an already `called` ticket is never called again. Ordering is `priority DESC, issued_at ASC, id ASC` (lowest `id` is the final tie-break). Modes map to `App\Enums\CallMode`: `Any = 'any'` (full ordering plus fairness), `PriorityOnly = 'priority_only'` (only `priority > 0`, full ordering, fairness ignored), `NormalOnly = 'normal_only'` (only `priority = 0`, oldest first, fairness ignored). Fairness applies in `any` mode only: the last 3 called tickets of the queue (most recent first by `called_at`, then `id`) are read — when all 3 exist, all 3 are priority tickets, and at least one normal ticket is waiting, the call is restricted to normal tickets (oldest normal wins). Calls made in any mode count in that history; a normal call resets the streak; when no normal is waiting, priority tickets keep being called. The queue row is locked in a transaction and its fresh `is_active` state decides: calling from an inactive queue throws `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException` and changes nothing (a stale passed-in model never overrides the database). When no ticket is eligible for the requested mode, `App\Exceptions\NoWaitingTicketsException` (extends `RuntimeException`) is thrown. Exactly-once: after locking the queue row, the ordered candidate ids are snapshotted, each candidate row is locked and re-checked for `waiting` (it may have been called concurrently through `Ticket::call()`, which does not lock the queue); stale winners are skipped. The winner is marked `called` with `called_at = now()` and `called_by_user_id`, touching only the write-once-allowed fields, and the returned model already reflects the call.
+
